{
  "$comment": "ADR-113 Amendment 4 fixture. JSON-RPC 2.0 POSTed to the daemon's OAuth listener with a bearer token, exactly as kb/query.* is. Clients branch on error.data.kind only; error.code is informative. Identifiers, hashes and times are examples; times are RFC 3339 UTC with milliseconds. Field names and kinds are normative.",
  "method": "kb/query.get",
  "description": "A revision read (ADR-113 D5): kb/query.get with `revision` returns the node's frozen revision, with its acts and attachments. Use it to read a revision's rendered_pdf hash (to pass as approve's rendered_pdf_sha256) and its signed_pdf. `attachments` lists every attachment in upload order, annulled ones included: `annulled` is null for a current one, else {at, by, reason} (B1). The current attachment of a kind is the newest one whose `annulled` is null. `url` is the blob route (GET/HEAD, bearer token, the KB's read access). Built in PR-4 (the revision read) and PR-6 (the attachments list). `acts` lists the capacity acts performed on the revision, in order, named as kb/review.act names them (`reviewed`, `approved`); the request and the attachments are in the event chain and in `attachments`. Each act carries `override`: null, or, when the actor acted past the soft block (D3, A3), {self_approval: [revision_id...], unknown_authors: [revision_id...], reason}: the revisions of the act it covered where the actor was an author, or whose authors could not be established, and the actor's override_reason.",
  "transport": {
    "http": "POST /",
    "headers": {
      "Authorization": "Bearer <the person's IdP access token for this daemon's audience>",
      "Content-Type": "application/json"
    }
  },
